ABOUT THE ROLE:

Join the power generation engineering team to design, commission, and maintain plant control systems. As a Controls Engineer, you will own BOP PLC/HMI and the control-room SCADA picture that brings generation and balance-of-plant into one operating view - Solar, 6000, and BOP on a single set of screens. You will work from control philosophy through commissioning and ongoing reliability, hands-on at the panel and in the control room. The position is based in Memphis, TN, with potential travel to other sites. &nbsp;

RESPONSIBILITIES: &nbsp;

• Own BOP PLC and HMI design, programming, and commissioning for power generation balance-of-plant systems (fuel gas, water, compressed/instrument air, HVAC, cooling, electrical auxiliaries, and related process/utility systems) &nbsp;

• Design and maintain the plant SCADA architecture so operators have one operating picture in the control room integrating Solar, 6000, and BOP - graphics, alarms, historian, and situational awareness on a single platform &nbsp;

• Develop control philosophy, control narratives, I/O lists, network drawings, cause-and-effect diagrams, and HMI/SCADA standards for reuse across the facility &nbsp;

• Specify PLC, HMI, SCADA, remote I/O, industrial networking, and interface hardware; define data exchange with OEM turbine/generation controllers (Solar and 6000) and with electrical protection, metering, and plant systems &nbsp;

• Program, test, and troubleshoot PLC logic and HMI applications (IEC 61131 - ladder, function block, structured text as applicable) &nbsp;

• Integrate OEM packages and third-party systems into plant SCADA using industrial protocols (Modbus, DNP3, OPC UA, IEC 61850, and others as required) so Solar, 6000, and BOP operate as one system &nbsp;

• Commission controls: I/O checkout, loop checks, functional testing, HMI validation, alarm rationalization, and start-up support; stay hands-on with technicians and operators &nbsp;

• Support day-to-day operations: troubleshooting, sequence issues, bad actors, and control changes under MOPs/MOC &nbsp;

• Maintain configuration management for PLC/HMI/SCADA programs, as-left files, firmware, and network documentation &nbsp;

• Coordinate with electrical, mechanical, fluids, protection, and operations so controls scope is fully integrated through construction, commissioning, and turnover &nbsp;

• Apply relevant standards for industrial control systems and electrical work (NFPA 70 / 70E, IEC 61131, and site cybersecurity/ICS practices such as NERC CIP where applicable) &nbsp;

BASIC QUALIFICATIONS: &nbsp;

• Bachelor’s degree in electrical engineering, controls engineering, computer engineering, or another engineering discipline &nbsp;

• 3+ years of experience in PLC, HMI, and/or SCADA engineering (design, programming, or commissioning) on industrial or power generation systems &nbsp;

PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE: &nbsp;

• 5+ years in a controls role at a power plant, independent power producer, OEM, EPC, or heavy industrial facility &nbsp;

